{
  "dom_id": "step-8908",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Naming Prisms",
  "problem": "What is the name of the polyhedron shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230697/assets/b6b4021c8add7d92bfbc98c23f9c9e56e4fd0c8fa152e60c04ca78c5c5b594cd.png)",
  "worked_solution": "The polyhedron is a **heptagonal prism** since it has two identical heptagonal faces connected by equal parallel line segments.\n\nAlso, notice that:\n\n- The solid is not an octagonal (pentagonal or hexagonal) prism since it does not have an octagonal (pentagonal or hexagonal)  base.\n\n- The solid is not a cube since not all of its faces are squares.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-8908\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"8908\" steptype=\"example\" contentid=\"2662\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    Example: \n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-8908\" class=\"stepAnchor\" style=\"font-weight: normal;\" name=\"step-3\">Naming Prisms</a> \n                </div>      \n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"8908\">?</div>\n            </div>\n            \n            <div class=\"exampleQuestion\">\n                <p>What is the name of the polyhedron shown below?</p>\n<p><br></p>\n<div id=\"graphic-1c238eb63a24655f9394b7ead716bf10\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/1c238eb63a24655f9394b7ead716bf10\"></div> \n            </div>     \n\n            <div class=\"explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div>\n\n            <div class=\"exampleExplanation\">\n                <p>The polyhedron is a <strong>heptagonal prism</strong> since it has two identical heptagonal faces connected by equal parallel line segments.</p>\n<p>Also, notice that:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The solid is not an octagonal (pentagonal or hexagonal) prism since it does not have an octagonal (pentagonal or hexagonal)  base.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The solid is not a cube since not all of its faces are squares.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n            </div>           \n        </div>",
